text Ushio buries herself under her futon, hugging a stuffed dango.
sound PBM.aac
text @[Ushio]
text Sing Mommy's song.
text And then, she begs me to do it.
text Ushio knows the once-popular song as her own mother's song.
text The first time I sang her the song, tears began to form in her eyes. She felt like she had heard it somewhere before.
text Could she remember?
text Her mother used to sing the song for her all the time.
text If she does, then good.
text That means she has at least one memory of spending time with her mom.
text A memory of when the three of us were together as a family.
text I look down and Ushio is asleep, quietly snoring.
text I stop singing and put the futon back up to her shoulders.
text @[Tomoya]
text Good night.
text I then slide back in to my own futon and look up at the ceiling.
