text @[Tomoya]
text Good morning.
text @[Tomoya]
text Please take good care of her.
text I hand Ushio over to the teacher.
sound PBN.aac
text @[Voice]
text Ah, Okazaki-san.
text The teacher calls out to me as I start to walk off.
text When I turn around, Ushio is already inside the room and speaking to a different teacher.
text @[Tomoya]
text Excuse me?
sound PBO.aac
text @[Teacher]
text I wanted to properly introduce myself to you... Do you have a moment?
text @[Tomoya]
text Oh, where are my manners. I didn't even introduce myself...
text @[Tomoya]
text Thank you as always for taking care of Ushio. My name is Okazaki.
sound PBP.aac
text @[Teacher]
text My name is Ichii, and I've been given the responsibility of Ushio-chan's class.
sound PBQ.aac
text @[Teacher]
text It's very nice to meet you.
text @[Tomoya]
text Same here.
text @[Tomoya]
text Is Ushio behaving all right?
sound PBR.aac
text @[Teacher]
text Yes, she's a very good girl, and she's friendly with all of the other children.
text Of course she is. Sanae-san raised her, after all.
sound PBS.aac
text @[Teacher]
text And she's been especially cheerful since summer vacation's ended.
sound PBT.aac
text @[Teacher]
text She must have had a great break.
text @[Tomoya]
text Yes... It's been an important summer for me too.
sound PBU.aac
text @[Teacher]
text I'm glad to hear that.
sound PBV.aac
text @[Teacher]
text I'm sure it's tough, but please keep doing what it is you're doing.
sound PBW.aac
text @[Teacher]
text If anything ever comes up, please tell me. I'd be happy to help you.
text I don't know how much she knows, but she seems to at least be aware of the fact that Ushio doesn't have a mother.
text @[Tomoya]
text Thank you very much. I appreciate that.
sound PBX.aac
text @[Teacher]
text I'm sorry for holding you up. Do you have work after this?
text @[Tomoya]
text Yes.
sound PBY.aac
text @[Teacher]
text Well, have a good day.
text @[Tomoya]
text You too. Goodbye.
text Once I turn around, I find the housewives who were gossiping about me yesterday chit-chatting.
text @[Tomoya]
text Good morning.
text I greet them and walk past.
text "Good morning," I can hear them say in response.
text If I keep applying myself, I'm sure everything will turn out. Slowly, probably... But turn out, all the same.
text If you let yourself be convinced that you're at your limits, you'll sink to the bottom.
text ...I think that's the way that it works in life.
